    <GaugingStation location="Panshanger Park" name="Mimram" number="38003">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Station located in the lower catchment of the River Mimram.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">One rating applied across period of record. Rating is reasonably accurate, though overestimates flow. Theoretical calibration confirmed by gaugings but computed flows may be slightly overestimated by as much as 10%. The gauge was reviewed in 2014.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Critical-depth flume; 5m wide. All flows are contained.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Frequent discharges caused by fish farm are eliminated to produce naturalised flows. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Appreciable net export of water. Considerable gw abstraction for industry &amp; agriculture occurs in the headwaters. Very high baseflow component but peak flows increasing due to urbanisation. AMAX is commonly recorded during the summer half-year.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">A predominantly permeable catchment (Upper Chalk overlain by glacial deposits near headwaters). Mainly rural but substantial urban growth in the lower valley - the Mimram drains Welwyn Garden City.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">GI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to within 18% of QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Although no gaugings beyond QMED, flows are well within wing walls and theoretical rating thought to be reliable." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
